# workspace-manifest.json has a BYTE-CANONICAL contract that prettier CANNOT satisfy, and a QG
# check (scripts/quality_gates/check_workspace_manifest_canonical.py:38) that hard-fails on any
# deviation. Canonical == `json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"`, which ALWAYS
# explodes every array element onto its own line. Prettier (printWidth=120) COLLAPSES any array
# that fits in 120 cols onto one line. The two can never agree, so every local commit that STAGED
# this file was silently reformatted into the non-canonical form by the `prettier-autostage` hook
# (.pre-commit-config.yaml:79-85 — `types_or` includes `json`) and RE-STAGED, i.e. AFTER the author
# had already run quality-gates.sh green. The author's verification could not see it.
#
# Measured 2026-07-17: 73c4449ae ("opt system-integration-tests into ldr_main") intended a ONE-LINE
# promotion_model edit and landed `1 file changed, 95 insertions(+), 431 deletions(-)` — prettier
# collapsing the whole file. That red-lined unified-trading-pm's LDR QG (runs 29576851453 /
# 29576964765 / 29577081402) until the LDR-CI-red monitor INCIDENTALLY healed it: its writer
# (ldr_ci_monitor.py:466-467) is canonical, so persisting one unrelated ldr_ci_status change
# re-exploded the file. That heal only fires when a level actually changes — otherwise PM stays
# RED indefinitely. This is a human-collapses / bot-explodes ping-pong going back to at least
# 2026-06-17 (3f2c6bc89, 06-30, was the exact same edit class).
#
# NOTE: check_workspace_manifest_canonical.py:13 and ci_status_consolidator.py:110-112 both claim
# prettier emits the canonical form. It does not — verified by running prettier on a canonical copy
# and re-checking. That false belief is why this hole stayed open. Fix the docstrings, not this rule.
workspace-manifest.json

# .code-workspace files hit the IDENTICAL failure mode as workspace-manifest.json above, discovered
# 2026-08-06 while adding a new repo entry: VS Code's .code-workspace format is JSONC (trailing
# commas allowed), and prettier's own JSONC formatting style ADDS a trailing comma after each
# object's last property — valid for VS Code, but strict `json.load` (used by
# check_workspace_code_workspace_drift.py and every hand-authoring script) rejects it outright
# (`Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes`). Confirmed the prettier-autostage hook
# reformatted ALL 9 files in one pass, including 3 the author never touched, corrupting them from
# valid to invalid JSON — the exact same "author-verified-green tree gets silently mutated after
# staging" class as the manifest bug above, just for a different file family.
cursor-configs/*.code-workspace

# plans/*.md hit the SAME "author-verified-green tree gets silently mutated after staging" class
# as the two entries above, for prose instead of JSON: prettier's markdown printer has a
# non-idempotent reflow bug for a 2nd+ paragraph nested inside a list item (each pass ADDS leading-
# space padding to continuation lines instead of converging — root-caused
# plans/archive/issues/prettier_prosewrap_mangles_long_inline_code_spans_2026_07_31.md, 2026-08-03).
# check_prosewrap_padding.sh (shrinking ratchet) was shipped to detect it, but detection-only could
# not keep pace with the corpus's commit velocity — direct proof gathered 2026-08-15
# (unified-trading-pm@c6639f0fe1 quality_gate_resolution dispatch, PR #3198's 529min-red wall): a
# same-commit fix that reduced 3 files' violation counts (46->6, 20->?, 12->?) was net INCREASED by
# this SAME commit's own prettier-autostage hook run (20->36, 12->81) — the hook was actively
# corrupting the exact lines the fix had just repaired, in the same commit, before the push. This
# is not concurrent-agent churn (that was the prior working theory across 10+ CI-wall dispatches,
# plans/active/issues/plan_hygiene_ratchet_regressions_outpace_serial_ci_fix_velocity_2026_08_09.md)
# — it reproduces solo, deterministically, every time prettier touches a staged plan doc with a
# nested-list continuation paragraph. Confirmed `proseWrap: preserve` (tested via a scoped
# .prettierrc override, reverted) does NOT prevent it — the bug is in prettier's list-item
# indentation normalization, not the proseWrap reflow specifically, so a proseWrap-only fix cannot
# help. Excluding plans/ from prettier entirely (this entry) is the only proven remedy for this bug
# class in this repo (see the two entries above). No functional/rendered-output loss: plan docs are
# operator/agent-authored prose, not consumer-facing formatted output.
plans/**/*.md
